If the Y half-step atom at depth n, bit-source i, and bit b is not junk, then the basic neighbourhood of its first-system index is contained in the basic neighbourhood of the atom-pair's first index.

A non-junk half-step atom forces the atom-pair junk flag to vanish. Code-state correctness identifies the first atom-pair neighbourhood with the generated first component. The half-step neighbourhood is contained in the first component of the generalized X-step, which is contained in that generated component.
